                <pb facs="0779" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg771"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Butrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-08-19T13:00:00+09:00">August 19, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 19—8:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>797. Department’s 371, August 18 [<hi rendition="#italic">19</hi>], 2 p.m.<anchor
                        n="25" xml:id="d840-f1"/> Admiral Hart had directed Colonel Peck to inform
                    the Defense Commanders and the Chairman of Municipal Council that pending the
                    outcome of negotiations between the American and Japanese Governments, the
                    United States Marines will postpone occupying “B” Sector.</p>
                <p>Vice Admiral Iwamura representing Admiral Shimada who has been conducting
                    informal negotiations with Rear Admiral Glassford representing Admiral Hart was
                    so informed. He seemed visibly relieved as he had previously stated that if the
                    American Marines were to move into Sector B the Japanese would take similar
                    action. He agreed that as an interim measure neither side should occupy Sector
                    B.</p>
                <p>It is expected that Shanghai Municipal Council will direct Shanghai Volunteer
                    Corps to occupy Sector B during interim period.</p>
                <p>I am informing my Japanese colleague in the sense of the first paragraph.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department and Tokyo, repeated to Chungking and Peiping. Department
                    please inform Navy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Butrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
